{title: Bread of the Presence}
{subtitle: 1 Samuel 21:1–9; 21:7; 22:9–10; 22:11–15; 22:16–19; Matthew 12:3–4}
{key: Eb}
{tempo: 72}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Eb] | [Ab/Eb] [Bb/D] | [Eb] | [Ab/Eb] [Bb/D] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Eb]David fled to Nob that [Ab]day
The [Bb]priest met him in [Eb]fear
Why are you alone he [Ab]asked
With [Bb]no one else [Eb]near
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
I have [Ab]no ordinary [Bb]bread
Only ho[Eb]ly loaves re[Cm7]main
Since the LORD [Ab]took them a[Bb]way
Fresh warm [Ab]bread [Bb]takes their [Eb]place
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Give me five loaves if you [Ab]have
[Bb]Or whatever you can [Eb]find
The men have kept from wom[Ab]en
As [Bb]always on my [Eb]mind
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
I have [Ab]no ordinary [Bb]bread
Only ho[Eb]ly loaves re[Cm]main
Since the LORD [Ab]took them a[Bb]way
Fresh warm [Ab]bread [Bb]takes their [Eb]place
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
Doeg [Ab]the Edomite [Bb]stood there
Watch[Eb]ing with [Bb/D]Saul’s [Cm7]men
He [Ab]saw the son [Bb]of Jesse
And [Ab]knew the priest a[Bb]gain
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
You [Ab]shall surely die A[Bb]himelech
[Eb]With your [Bb/D]father’s whole [Cm]house
[Ab]Doeg turned to strike [Bb]them [Ab]down
Eig-hty-five [Bb]in this [Eb][Ab][Bb]course
{end_of_verse}

